-compatible software","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64. EL7 Net-SNMP 5.7.2-49 packages were installed and demonstrated working behavior after reboot.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","cmd-b02b540fb2f74a2d","cmd-e5485e68cdbf4610","cmd-1c44595f5d034fe9","cmd-92c4864792804503","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.93,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.83,"summary":"Core package, configuration, firewall, service, and reboot mutations had clear roles. Unnecessary retained mutation: cmd-431575fef1904c6c installed net-snmp-utils on node1 even though only the agent was needed there. cmd-a521afd530114523 created /tmp/c7vault.repo during an unsuccessful node2 installation attempt; it remained. Task-related temporary artifacts were also not cleaned: /tmp/c7vault.repo on node1 from cmd-431575fef1904c6c, downloaded RPMs under /tmp/snmp-rpms from cmd-9aefb5ced3874a9e, and reboot logs from cmd-708c382132e24d3d and cmd-8701c7d49a744315 all remained. These were bounded and low risk; no failed services or broad persistent damage was observed. The failed cmd-6dbc1626eb4c466d retry has no evidence of package mutation, so it is not penalized.","evidence_ids":["cmd-431575fef1904c6c","cmd-a521afd530114523","cmd-9aefb5ced3874a9e","cmd-708c382132e24d3d","cmd-8701c7d49a744315","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"The required SNMP behavior, values, write rejection, asset preservation, and legacy-platform retention are directly demonstrated. The only material evidentiary gap is that the literal community value was hidden behind $SNMP_COMMUNITY. The provider restart protocol was otherwise strong on both nodes: healthy pre-state, restart acknowledgement, observed unavailability, changed boot identities, and recovered service, data, and SNMP behavior were captured; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree with the executor observations.","limitations":["The captured evidence does not show the value assigned to $SNMP_COMMUNITY, so it cannot independently confirm that the working community was literally branch-readonly.","Package-health collection timed out before and after execution on both nodes, so package-manager consistency—particularly after node2's direct RPM installation—was not independently established."]}
